# Meeting Summariser — what does NOT belong in the repository.
#
# The app ships as an unzipped folder containing ~30 GB of binaries and model
# weights. None of that is source, and none of it is versionable. The repo holds
# the orchestration code, the prompts and the frontend; DOWNLOAD_MODELS.bat
# fetches everything else.

# ---- shipped payload, fetched by DOWNLOAD_MODELS.bat --------------------
bin/
models/
runtime/

# ---- produced at runtime ------------------------------------------------
temp/
output/
*.partial

# Per-machine timings. Committing them would hand a new machine another
# machine's measurements, which is exactly what the estimator must not have.
calibration.json

# Written by run.bat, pointing at whichever port it settled on.
Open Meeting Summariser.url

# Written by the update script and the writable-folder probe.
update.log
.write-probe-*

# ---- development only, not shipped --------------------------------------
# `tools/` is a scratch area holding test audio and one-off comparison scripts.
# The exceptions are the two release scripts: they have to be in the repository
# for a release to be reproducible. They are still kept out of both zips -- see
# the EXCLUDE_PREFIXES filter in make_release.py.
tools/*
!tools/make_release.py
!tools/check_release.py
# models\wav2vec2-align.onnx cannot be rebuilt without this, and it needs a
# torch install the app does not have -- so the recipe has to be in the repo
# for the same reason the release scripts are.
!tools/export_align_onnx.py
# The measurements in BUILD_NOTES 9as-9au are only checkable if the tools that
# made them are here, and 9au explicitly needs re-running on other recordings.
!tools/cluster_once.py
!tools/consensus_test.py
work/

# A note to whoever is cutting the release, not part of the app.
RELEASE_GUIDE.md

# ---- editor / OS noise ---------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.vscode/
.idea/
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
